Package: aqsurface
Title: Spatial Interpolation Surfaces for Urban Air Quality Monitoring
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Hyesop",
           family = "Shin",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "hyesop.shin@auckland.ac.nz")
Description: Reproducible workflow for comparing spatial interpolation methods
    (universal kriging via 'gstat' and generalised additive models via 'mgcv')
    on hourly air pollutant concentrations from urban monitoring networks.
    Provides functions for variogram fitting with sensible fallbacks, batch
    prediction over multi-day series, optional post-processing of road-side
    concentrations, and station-level validation against held-out monitors.
    Companion code for a planned R Journal article on spatial interpolation
    of PM10 and NO2 in Seoul, South Korea.
